Requirement 03.05.07 — Password Complexity
Enforce a minimum password complexity and change of characters when new passwords are created.
03.05.07.d: Minimum password change of character requirements as defined are enforced when new passwords are created

Assessment objectives (a coverage checklist — do NOT copy their wording):
- minimum password change of character requirements as defined are enforced when new passwords are created

Evidence excerpts:
--- [IT-POL-004_Password_and_Authenticator_Management_v3.2.docx] (excerpt)
4.3 Password Construction and Change
When a user creates a new password, or one is set for them, it must meet all of the following:
- At least 14 characters for standard accounts and 16 for privileged accounts.
- At least one uppercase letter, one lowercase letter, one number and one special character.
- At least 4 characters must be different from the current password, counted by position. Adding or changing only one or two characters at the end (for example, changing "Solder#Line2024" to "Solder#Line2025") is not allowed.
- Must not match any of the last 24 passwords.
The IT Manager enforces these rules in the JumpCloud organization password policy, which covers all directory accounts and passwords synced to endpoints and Microsoft 365 GCC High. The same rules are set in the local administrator password profile on the PA-440 firewalls. The IT Manager checks both configurations every quarter and records the result in Freshservice.
--- [PA-440_HQ_running-config_mgmt-excerpt_2024-09-12.txt] (excerpt)
deviceconfig {
  system {
    hostname FW-HQ-01;
  }
}
mgt-config {
  password-complexity {
    enabled yes;
    minimum-length 16;
    minimum-uppercase-letters 1;
    minimum-lowercase-letters 1;
    minimum-numeric-letters 1;
    minimum-special-characters 1;
    block-repeated-characters 2;
    block-username-inclusion yes;
    new-password-differs-by-characters 4;
    password-change-on-first-login yes;
    password-history-count 24;
    password-change {
      expiration-period 0;
    }
  }
}
# exported by: netadmin (IT Manager) via 'show config running' | committed 2024-09-03 14:22 | change ref CHG-0187
--- [Freshservice_CHG-0212_Q3_Password_Policy_Verification.pdf] (excerpt)
Change CHG-0212: Quarterly password policy verification, Q3
Requester: IT Manager | Assigned: Systems Administrator | Closed: 2024-09-27

Test 1 (JumpCloud): Test account svc-pwtest@ was given the password "Reflow!Oven-7731". Through the JumpCloud User Portal, we tried to change it to "Reflow!Oven-7732", which differs by 1 character. This was REJECTED with the message "New password must differ from current by at least 4 characters." We then tried "Reflow!Kiln-4419", which differs by 8 characters. This was ACCEPTED. Screenshot attached.
Test 2 (FW-HQ-01 and FW-PLANT-01): For local account pwtest, we tried to change the password to a value that differed by 2 characters. Both firewalls REJECTED it with "New password should differ from old password by at least 4 characters." A value that differed by 6 characters was accepted.
Test 3: Blumira showed both rejected attempts as JumpCloud password_change failure events and PAN-OS system log events.
Result: All checks passed. The test account was disabled after testing.

