Requirement 03.01.20 — External Connections
Verify and control/limit connections to and use of external systems.
03.01.20.d: The use of external systems is verified

Assessment objectives (a coverage checklist — do NOT copy their wording):
- the use of external systems is verified

Evidence excerpts:
--- [External_System_Use_Procedure_v2.3.docx] (excerpt)
4.2 Approval of External Systems
No employee may process or store company data on a non-company system (personal laptops, customer portals, carrier TMS platforms, or third-party file shares) until the request is approved. To request access, open a Zendesk ticket using the "External System Request" form. The IT Manager confirms the system owner, the type of data involved, and whether the connection runs through the PA-440 GlobalProtect gateway. Requests involving CUI must also be approved by the Compliance Lead. Approved systems go into the External Systems Register with a review date no more than 12 months after approval. Requests without a register entry are denied by default.
